    "q-77803": {
      "dom_id": "step-q77803",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $3$rd row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using cofactor expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{31}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+4\\cdot {C}_{33}+3\\cdot {C}_{34} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot (-1)^{3+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the first $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+(-2)\\cdot {C}_{22}+(-4)\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-4)\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(6-0)+4(0-2) \\\\  & =-12-8 \\\\  & =-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the second  $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot {C}_{31}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+-1\\cdot {C}_{33} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-6+2)-(-6-0) \\\\  & =-4+6 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=4(-20)-3(2)=-86.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
