      "problem": "$|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -7 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -8 & -9 & 4\\end{aligned}|=$",
      "worked_solution": "Using a cofactor expansion along the $2$nd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -7 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -8 & -9 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{12}+(-7)\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+(-8)\\cdot {C}_{42} \\\\  & =(-7)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -9 & 4\\end{aligned}|+(-8)\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -9 & 4\\end{aligned}|-8\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
