      "problem": "$|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -7 & 2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}|=$",
      "worked_solution": "Using a cofactor expansion along the $1$st column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -7 & 2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+-7\\cdot {C}_{21}+0\\cdot {C}_{31}+0\\cdot {C}_{41} \\\\  & =(-7)\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
